# CODEOWNERS — mechanical separation of duties (NIST AC-5, CM-5, AIC-2)
#
# CODEOWNERS is what turns "the author doesn't approve" from a convention into a control.
# Combined with branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners" + "Dismiss stale
# approvals" + no administrator bypass), a PR cannot merge without an approval from an
# identity other than the author.
#
# Base repo: single owner. Forks get their org substituted by scripts/bootstrap.sh.
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — every change needs an engineering review by a non-author
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
